  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;be two independent events. The probability that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;happen is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> and the probability that neither&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>&nbsp;nor&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;happens is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> , then a value of <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math> is:",
